WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.035 --> 00:00:03.202
(audience applauding)

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.507
- It's so awesome to have you!
- How are you?

00:00:05.507 --> 00:00:06.767
- I'm so good!

00:00:06.767 --> 00:00:08.048
- I've been cheering for you-
- [Kelly] Congratulations!

00:00:08.048 --> 00:00:09.720
- I been cheering for you a long time so.

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:10.590
- Oh, that's so nice!

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:11.423
I'm a big fan as well.

00:00:11.423 --> 00:00:13.140
I wanna talk about the
cover of your album,

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:14.250
this is adorable.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:15.330
Wait, let's see the cover.

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:17.100
This is you on the album cover, right?

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.240
- Yeah!
(laughing)

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:19.814
This nine year old little
mischievous guy there.

00:00:19.814 --> 00:00:21.119
(audience cooing)
- [Kelly] Look!

00:00:21.119 --> 00:00:22.350
Look at you!

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:24.155
- The horns and the halo were authentic.

00:00:24.155 --> 00:00:24.988
(audience laughing)

00:00:24.988 --> 00:00:26.280
- You still got the boyish thing, though.

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:27.470
The horns and the halo, you were good-

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:28.860
- Yeah, I wore both of it.
- That's my son, too.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:29.693
Yeah.

00:00:29.693 --> 00:00:32.040
- I'm determined not to let
the 12-year-old in me die.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:32.880
- Me too.
- Yeah.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:33.930
- No, I think that's,

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.750
when you like stop growing,
you stop really living,

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:38.460
like I'm a total child about things.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:39.855
- You gotta keep that imagination alive.

00:00:39.855 --> 00:00:40.688
- Yeah.

00:00:40.688 --> 00:00:42.420
(audience clapping)
Let go, yeah.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.504
We get so serious as adults.

00:00:44.504 --> 00:00:45.620
I love that.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.640
So your name Killer Mike,
so where did that come from?

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:48.473
- I did not-

00:00:48.473 --> 00:00:49.560
I would've named me Handsome Mike or-

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:50.730
- Yes, I like it.

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:51.720
I like it.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:52.830
- So I had friends,

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:54.570
in rap you have posses or friends,

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:56.501
boys just naturally group together

00:00:56.501 --> 00:00:58.504
and do stinky stuff, right?
- Yes.

00:00:58.504 --> 00:01:00.690
- Either you're in the boy scouts

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:01.680
or you're a football player.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:02.948
I was good at none of that.

00:01:02.948 --> 00:01:03.840
(audience laughing)

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.310
And so I found my way with rapping

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:07.920
and my friends were like the
best rappers in the world to me

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.870
and there was one battle-

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:11.700
If you guys have seen 8 Mile,

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.350
there's a battle rap-
(audience cheering)

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:15.600
And guys didn't show up,

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:16.883
and other guys were just attacking my guys

00:01:16.883 --> 00:01:17.940
but I'm like,

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:19.140
you know they're not there.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.930
And I got angry as the kid in the group

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:24.690
and I just rapped against
everybody and slashed them.

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:25.563
It was like a Thor movie.
- Oh.

00:01:25.563 --> 00:01:27.903
(audience cheering)
You used it as fuel.

00:01:27.903 --> 00:01:28.736
I love it.

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:31.050
I'm so impressed by that.

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:32.340
Like that off the cuff-

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:33.600
like, that's incredible to me.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:35.400
- I can't do it anymore
but when I was young,

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:36.600
it was amazing.
(audience laughing)

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:37.723
- I could never do it.

00:01:37.723 --> 00:01:38.790
I was like, I'm so impressed.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:41.410
It's a wonder I ever remember
lyrics ever, in general.

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:43.110
- I got the name that night, though.

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:45.551
A guy stopped the party, a
guy named Double D and said,

00:01:45.551 --> 00:01:46.650
this kid's a killer.

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:48.570
And after that, no one ever
called me just Mike again.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:49.941
It was Killer Mike.
- Aww.

00:01:49.941 --> 00:01:50.774
(audience clapping)

00:01:50.774 --> 00:01:52.530
That's awesome.

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:53.363
So, you've won Grammys,

00:01:53.363 --> 00:01:55.440
but what is being nominated by your peers,

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:56.400
that's a different kind of thing.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:57.233
What does that mean for you?

00:01:57.233 --> 00:01:59.070
- Yeah, I currently have an altar

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:00.330
for my grandmother in my house

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:01.470
and the Grammy,

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:03.180
my first Grammy is broken,

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:04.620
because I kept it at her house.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:07.170
I dropped out of Morehouse
and I told her in exchange for

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:09.268
dropping out and not bringing
her a college degree,

00:02:09.268 --> 00:02:10.500
I gave her a Grammy.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.465
She said it still ain't no degree and uh-

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:13.802
(audience laughing)
- Oh she said, next!

00:02:13.802 --> 00:02:14.880
- She, education cared.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:16.530
But she kept it in her house.

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:17.825
And I remember going to her
house one day and saying,

00:02:17.825 --> 00:02:19.230
"Mama, where's the Grammy?

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:20.460
I don't see it."
- Yeah.

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:21.750
- And she put it in her closet.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:22.920
I was like, "Why is it in the closet?"

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:24.660
Now, only our family is in the house.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:27.361
She looked around and
said, "Cause people steal."

00:02:27.361 --> 00:02:28.194
(audience laughing)

00:02:28.194 --> 00:02:30.217
And I'm like, but they're our people.

00:02:30.217 --> 00:02:31.515
"They still steal."

00:02:31.515 --> 00:02:33.300
(audience laughing)

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:34.530
She, apparently,

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:36.420
a week or two later, she
dropped it and broke it

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:37.620
and she was ashamed to show me

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:38.883
and my sister told me to talk to her,

00:02:38.883 --> 00:02:40.350
so I go and I talk to her,

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:41.220
I said, "Lemme see it."

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:42.053
And it's broken.

00:02:42.053 --> 00:02:42.960
I said, "Mama, I love you."

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:43.793
It's not-

00:02:43.793 --> 00:02:46.080
So I've never allowed
the Grammys to repair it.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:49.470
But now it's time to get a
few more to keep it company.

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:50.337
- Look at that, yeah.

00:02:50.337 --> 00:02:51.170
(audience clapping)

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:52.003
Just put a few more up there.

00:02:52.003 --> 00:02:52.836
(Killer Mike laughing)

00:02:52.836 --> 00:02:54.139
A family of Grammys.
- Exactly.

00:02:54.139 --> 00:02:55.139
- I like it.

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:59.160
- And as an artist, your audience matter,

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:00.840
your fellow artists matter,

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:01.673
but I'm not gonna lie,

00:03:01.673 --> 00:03:03.930
this year getting Rap Album of the Year

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:05.190
will mean everything in the world to me

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:07.500
because in the 50th year of hip hop,

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:10.200
I know for a fact I've made
the greatest representation

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.634
of hip hop this year.
- Yeah.

00:03:11.634 --> 00:03:12.467
(audience clapping)

00:03:12.467 --> 00:03:16.020
I love that certainty and
that confidence, yeah.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:19.230
- I've made something that speaks to,

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:20.063
not only,

00:03:20.063 --> 00:03:20.962
I grew up-

00:03:20.962 --> 00:03:22.050
this little nine-year-old chubby Black kid

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:24.120
in this Black enclave in the Deep South,

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:25.770
but I grew up influenced by this music

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:27.570
that was self-organized by kids.

00:03:27.570 --> 00:03:30.600
Kids in the South Bronx
self-organized around art,

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:33.720
dance, DJ, graffiti, MC-ing,

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.130
and they created a way out.

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:38.010
And my album honors that in a way

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:39.480
that none of the competition does,

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:40.500
and I love those guys.

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:42.270
Each of them are amazing and remarkable.

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:43.103
- Yeah.

00:03:43.103 --> 00:03:45.060
- But in my opinion, and in
the opinion of the people

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:46.140
who are chiming in,

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:47.760
shouts out to Charlamagne for doing that.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:51.180
There's no more cohesive
album for me that represents

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:52.533
the 50 years of hip hop.

00:03:52.533 --> 00:03:54.120
(audience clapping)
- Absolutely.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.127
Well let's do a commercial
break, everybody.

00:03:56.127 --> 00:03:58.860
The Grammy-nominated
album, Michael, is out now.

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:00.870
Find it wherever you get
your music, go check it out.

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:02.490
We'll be right back with some more of

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:04.990
our holiday gift guide,
you're welcome in advance.

